Zero errors. Here's what was done:

**`web/index.html`** — added the verification panel markup (button `#verify-btn` and result container `#verify-result`) inside the query panel, after the answer card.

**`web/styles.css`** — added `.verify-panel`, `#verify-btn`, `.verify-result`, `.verify-summary`, `.verify-elapsed`, `.verify-dots`, `.vdot.pass/.fail`, `.verify-failures` styles consistent with the existing dark lab theme.

**`src/ui/main.ts`** — added the import of `EXAM66` from `./exam-data.js` and `runVerification()`, which:
- disables the button during the run,
- records `performance.now()` before and after the loop,
- for each of the 66 items calls `answerQuestion(table, item.question)` and checks all three pass conditions (status = `ANSWER`, answer matches after whitespace normalisation, evidence set matches exactly by `row:col` keys),
- renders the summary (`passed/66 passed`), elapsed time as `measured in <x> ms` with one decimal from the actual measurement, 66 green/red dots, and the list of failing ids if any,
- is wired to `#verify-btn` click and auto-runs when `?verify=1` is in the URL.

